@lang en
IMPORT prelude

-- ===========================================================================
-- IL-07: the refusals the capstone itself owns.
--
-- Each one marks a place where the household needs something no composed row
-- encodes, or where the text does not decide (GAPS.md lists the provisions, in
-- the order the capstone needs them; NOTES.md the forks), or, from version
-- 0.2.0, where a composed row has a known defect that could change the answer
-- (each such refusal names the finding). A refusal a ROW owns is never restated
-- here: it reaches the caller from the row, through its adapter, in the row's
-- own words.
--
-- VERSION 0.2.0 (2026-10-07) removed three refusals for provisions row IL-08
-- now encodes (ITO s 40(b), s 65, NII s 72), rewrote the unencoded-credit
-- refusal (its 0.1.0 words named ss 35, 45A and 47 as unencoded), and reworded
-- two: the period's, which counted the composed rows, and fork K3's, which now
-- names the s 45A credit. NOTES.md section 11 lists each with its old wording.
--
-- VERSION 0.4.0 (2026-10-08, BACKLOG IL-44) removed the decline of row IL-08's
-- D190, now its own fork F35 (NOTES.md section 13).
--
-- VERSION 0.3.0 (2026-10-08, BACKLOG IL-22) removed five: the four that declined
-- row IL-08's known defects D187, D183, D055 and observation 1, which row IL-08
-- has repaired (its versions 0.2.0 and 0.3.0), and fork K15's, which row IL-06's
-- new month question makes unnecessary (its version 0.2.0). It added two: the
-- Encouragement of Aliyah and Return (Temporary Provision) Law 5786-2026, which no
-- row encodes (the second independent pass, finding F1), and a fact the household
-- does not hold for the spouse (row IL-02's new foreign-worker field). NOTES.md
-- section 12 lists each with its words.
--
-- This module imports no row, so the adapters and the pipeline can all use it.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `IL-07 — the capstone's own refusals`

§§ `The period`

-- 2026 is the one period all the composed rows answer (NOTES.md section 3):
-- IL-02 answers tax years from 2024; IL-03's s 121 tax years 2026-2027 and
-- s 121B from 2026; IL-04 and IL-05 contribution months from January 2026, and
-- 2027 only on figures the caller supplies; IL-06 days from 1 May 2015 to
-- 31 December 2026; IL-01 any year for which the credit-point value is
-- supplied; IL-08 tax years from 2024 (its ITO half), and months from May 2015
-- (s 72) and contribution periods from January 2026 (s 335) (its NII half).
@ref NOTES.md section 3, "The period"; the rows' own year gates
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-07 answers months of 2026 only, the one period all its composed rows answer` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-07 answers months of 2026 only, the one period all its composed rows answer"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-07: a month of the year is numbered from 1 to 12` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-07: a month of the year is numbered from 1 to 12"

§§ `The household`

@ref NOTES.md fork K4; BRIEF.md, "The household"
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-07 composes a household with one earner; a spouse with taxable income is outside it` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-07 composes a household with one earner; a spouse with taxable income is outside it"

-- Version 0.3.0 (second independent pass, finding F3): reached only where the
-- salary is below the full adult monthly minimum wage of the quarter's first
-- month; at or above it no minimum wage the earner could have binds, and the
-- deduction is answered on the salary (il07-adapter-il05.l4).
@ref NII Schedule K "שכר מינימום" (source line 4772), as row IL-05 reads it (its fork F11)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-07 holds Schedule K's minimum only for an employee to whom the full monthly minimum wage of an adult applies` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-07 holds Schedule K's minimum only for an employee to whom the full monthly minimum wage of an adult applies"

-- Reached only by an adapter given no Part D age for a woman; from version
-- 0.2.0 the pipeline always gives the age row IL-08 computes.
@ref NII s 342(c)(2) (source line 3662); Schedule A1 Part D (source lines 4431-4453)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the earner is a woman, and the age Part D of Schedule A1 fixes for her is not given` MEANS
    REFUSE "the earner is a woman, and the age Part D of Schedule A1 fixes for her is not given"

-- Finding M1 of the independent pass (INDEPENDENT-FINDINGS.md): row IL-06 tells
-- the persons and the children of a family apart by name, and reports two of
-- one name as "a problem with the facts" without saying which. The IL-06
-- adapter now says why.
@ref row IL-06, `a problem with the facts of` (nii-il06-family-on-a-day.l4); INDEPENDENT-FINDINGS.md M1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`two children of the household have the same name; row IL-06 tells children apart by name, so give each child a name of its own` MEANS
    REFUSE "two children of the household have the same name; row IL-06 tells children apart by name, so give each child a name of its own"

@ref row IL-06, `a problem with the facts of` (nii-il06-family-on-a-day.l4); INDEPENDENT-FINDINGS.md M1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the earner and the spouse have the same name; row IL-06 tells the persons of a family apart by name, so give each a name of their own` MEANS
    REFUSE "the earner and the spouse have the same name; row IL-06 tells the persons of a family apart by name, so give each a name of their own"

§§ `The Income Tax Ordinance: what no row encodes, or the household does not give`

-- Version 0.2.0. The credits and deductions IL-07 computes are those of ITO
-- ss 34, 35, 36, 36A, 37-39, 40(b), 45A, 47 and 66(c). The 0.1.0 wording ("no
-- composed row encodes, such as section 35, 45A or 47") is no longer true of
-- those three, so the refusal now says both things the earner's FALSE can mean.
@ref ITO ss 39A-40D, 44-46, 47A (source lines 1609-1630, 1648-1762, 1791-1797), not encoded; ss 35, 45A, 47 (row IL-08)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the earner has a credit or deduction under the Income Tax Ordinance that IL-07 does not compute: it computes sections 35, 45A and 47 only from the further facts of its version 0.2.0, and no composed row encodes the others, such as section 39A, 44 or 46` MEANS
    REFUSE "the earner has a credit or deduction under the Income Tax Ordinance that IL-07 does not compute: it computes sections 35, 45A and 47 only from the further facts of its version 0.2.0, and no composed row encodes the others, such as section 39A, 44 or 46"

-- Version 0.3.0. Row IL-02's `A spouse` records whether the spouse is a foreign
-- worker within s 48A, which s 66(c)(4)'s half point reads (its repair 02-R2).
-- The household records it for the earner only; the spouse has no income and the
-- capstone computes none of the spouse's credits, so the spouse's field is never
-- read. It is this refusal, not a guessed FALSE, so that a reading would say so.
@ref ITO s 48A (source line 1811), s 66(c)(4) (source line 2465), row IL-02
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-07 holds no foreign-worker fact for the earner's spouse, and computes none of the spouse's own credits` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-07 holds no foreign-worker fact for the earner's spouse, and computes none of the spouse's own credits"

-- Version 0.5.0. Row IL-02's version 0.4.0 records on `A spouse` whether the
-- spouse is an Israeli resident in the tax year, for s 36A (its fork F20), which
-- s 66(c)(4)'s half point reads. As above: the household holds the fact for the
-- earner only, and the spouse's field is never read.
@ref ITO s 36A (source line 1597), s 66(c)(4) (source line 2465), row IL-02 v0.4.0 fork F20
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-07 holds no residence fact under the Income Tax Ordinance for the earner's spouse, and computes none of the spouse's own credits` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-07 holds no residence fact under the Income Tax Ordinance for the earner's spouse, and computes none of the spouse's own credits"

-- Version 0.3.0 (second independent pass, finding F1). The Economic Efficiency
-- Law 5786-2026, ch D s 9 (Sefer HaChukim 3511, pp. 416-418; the deposited
-- 25_lsr_12235101.pdf, PDF pp. 4-6), enacts the Encouragement of Aliyah and
-- Return (Temporary Provision) Law 5786-2026. Its s 2(a) exempts from tax the
-- "qualifying income" (income from personal exertion under ITO s 2(1) or (2)) of
-- "עולה שהיה לתושב ישראל לראשונה בתקופה החל ביום י"ד בחשוון התשפ"ו (5 בנובמבר
-- 2025) ועד תום שנת המס 2026 ותושב חוזר ותיק שהיה לתושב ישראל בתקופה האמורה", in
-- tax years 2026 to 2030, up to 600,000 in 2026 (s 2(a)(1)), pro rata to the
-- part of 2026 the person was resident (s 2(d)), "אלא אם כן ביקשו אחרת". No
-- composed row encodes it (BACKLOG IL-36, deferred), and the capstone holds
-- neither the election not to be exempt nor the day of first residence: it
-- declines an earner whose immigration facts put the immigration, or the return,
-- in that period (il07-pipeline.l4).
@ref Encouragement of Aliyah and Return (Temporary Provision) Law 5786-2026, ss 1-2, 6 (Economic Efficiency Law 5786-2026 ch D s 9; Sefer HaChukim 3511 pp. 416-418); INDEPENDENT-FINDINGS-2.txt F1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Encouragement of Aliyah and Return (Temporary Provision) Law 5786-2026 exempts from tax the income from personal exertion of an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident, or a veteran returning resident who became one, from 5 November 2025 to the end of tax year 2026; no composed row encodes it, and the earner's immigration falls in that period` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Encouragement of Aliyah and Return (Temporary Provision) Law 5786-2026 exempts from tax the income from personal exertion of an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident, or a veteran returning resident who became one, from 5 November 2025 to the end of tax year 2026; no composed row encodes it, and the earner's immigration falls in that period"

-- ITO s 64B, s 65 (row IL-08) with s 66 (row IL-02): with no separate
-- calculation the couple's income is charged in the registered spouse's name.
-- Where that spouse is not the earner, the credits in the calculation are that
-- spouse's (IL-01's ss 34-36A, IL-08's ss 35 and 37-39), and the household
-- holds the facts they read only for the earner.
@ref ITO s 65 (source line 2448), row IL-08; NOTES.md fork K4
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the couple's income is charged under section 65 in the name of the registered spouse, who is not the earner; IL-07 holds the facts the credits in that calculation read only for the earner` MEANS
    REFUSE "the couple's income is charged under section 65 in the name of the registered spouse, who is not the earner; IL-07 holds the facts the credits in that calculation read only for the earner"

-- ITO s 40(b) (row IL-08) gives a parent without a spouse the children's credit
-- points, on facts the household record does not hold.
@ref ITO s 40(b) (source lines 1632-1647), row IL-08
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the earner has no spouse and has children; section 40(b) gives their credit points, and the household does not give the single-parent facts it reads` MEANS
    REFUSE "the earner has no spouse and has children; section 40(b) gives their credit points, and the household does not give the single-parent facts it reads"

@ref ITO s 40(b) (source lines 1632-1647), row IL-08
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the single-parent facts give no entry, or more than one, for a child of the household; each child needs exactly one, under its own name` MEANS
    REFUSE "the single-parent facts give no entry, or more than one, for a child of the household; each child needs exactly one, under its own name"

-- ITO s 37 (row IL-08). From version 0.2.0 the point is s 37's answer on the
-- statuses it reads, not an input.
@ref ITO s 37 (source line 1600), row IL-08; NOTES.md fork K11
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the household says the earner would be entitled to a credit point under section 37 but does not give the statuses section 37 reads` MEANS
    REFUSE "the household says the earner would be entitled to a credit point under section 37 but does not give the statuses section 37 reads"

@ref ITO s 37 (source line 1600), row IL-08; NOTES.md fork K11
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the couple's record and section 37, on the statuses the household gives, disagree on whether the earner is entitled to a credit point under section 37` MEANS
    REFUSE "the couple's record and section 37, on the statuses the household gives, disagree on whether the earner is entitled to a credit point under section 37"

@ref ITO s 47(a)(4) (source line 1771), row IL-08
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the insured income the household gives is negative or more than the salary` MEANS
    REFUSE "the insured income the household gives is negative or more than the salary"

-- ITO s 164 (source lines 5322-5324) withholds tax from salary "in the manner and
-- at the rates prescribed"; the Income Tax (Deduction from Salary and Wages)
-- Regulations 5753-1993 (noted at source line 5338) are not in the source bundle.
@ref ITO s 164 (source line 5323); the 5753-1993 Regulations (source line 5338), not in the source bundle; NOTES.md fork K1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-07 apportions the tax for the year to a month only where the salary is the same in every month; withholding under section 164 of the Income Tax Ordinance is not encoded` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-07 apportions the tax for the year to a month only where the salary is the same in every month; withholding under section 164 of the Income Tax Ordinance is not encoded"

-- NOTES.md forks K3 and K17: neither s 33A, s 45A nor s 121B says whether credit
-- points, or the s 45A credit, are set off against the additional tax. Reached
-- only where the credits exceed the s 121 tax and there is additional tax, which
-- no household of the capstone's shape reaches; declined there rather than
-- guessed. (Version 0.2.0 added the s 45A credit to the words.)
@ref ITO s 33A (source line 1563), s 45A (source lines 1714-1739), s 121B (source lines 4455-4465); NOTES.md forks K3, K17
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the credits exceed the tax under section 121 and there is additional tax under section 121B; the text does not say whether credit points, or the credit under section 45A, are set off against the additional tax` MEANS
    REFUSE "the credits exceed the tax under section 121 and there is additional tax under section 121B; the text does not say whether credit points, or the credit under section 45A, are set off against the additional tax"

§§ `Row IL-08's known defects: declined where they could change the answer`

-- (Version 0.3.0 removed the refusals for row IL-08's defects D187 and D183, s 45A's
-- floor lost after the 1.5% proviso and life insurance alone declined in words that
-- did not fit: row IL-08 repaired both in its version 0.2.0, and the IL-08 adapter
-- passes its answer on. Their words are in NOTES.md section 12.)

-- (Version 0.4.0 removed the refusal for row IL-08's findings D190 and D236, "the
-- earner has a deduction under section 47 as well as sums section 45A credits, and
-- which takes a payment first is not settled, row IL-08's known defect D190; IL-07
-- declines": Meng ruled the order on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG, row IL-08's fork F35), and
-- row IL-08's version 0.4.0 declines, in its own words, only where the order changes
-- the answer. NOTES.md section 13.)

-- (Version 0.3.0 removed the refusals for row IL-08's defect D055, a second
-- immigration answered as 0 points, and its observation 1, two points moved by
-- the s 40(b)(1A1) election: row IL-08 repaired both in its version 0.2.0 (it now
-- declines a second immigration itself, in its own words). NOTES.md section 12.)

§§ `The National Insurance Law: what the household does not give, or the rows cannot meet`

@ref NII s 342(c)(2) (source line 3662); Schedule A1 Part D (source lines 4431-4453), row IL-08
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the age under Part D of Schedule A1 the household gives for the earner is not the age Part D fixes for her month of birth` MEANS
    REFUSE "the age under Part D of Schedule A1 the household gives for the earner is not the age Part D fixes for her month of birth"

-- NII s 335 (row IL-08) reads statuses only the Institute records. Where the
-- caller gives none, an earner resident in Israel and insured under Chapter 11
-- is taken as version 0.1.0 took every employee (NOTES.md fork K16); for any
-- other earner the branches cannot be told.
@ref NII s 335 (source lines 3610-3620), row IL-08; NOTES.md fork K16
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the household does not give the earner's insurance statuses, which section 335 reads, and the earner is not resident in Israel and insured under Chapter 11` MEANS
    REFUSE "the household does not give the earner's insurance statuses, which section 335 reads, and the earner is not resident in Israel and insured under Chapter 11"

-- (Version 0.2.0 declined here, in this row's words, an earner who does not pay
-- in all six deduction branches at the printed totals. Version 0.2.1 leaves it to
-- row IL-04, whose own switch now declines it: NOTES.md section 11.14.)

-- (Version 0.3.0 removed fork K15's refusal, "section 72 pays the allowance for
-- this month for children of the household whom row IL-06, which answers a day,
-- counts together on no day of the month": row IL-06's version 0.2.0 answers a
-- month for the children s 72 pays for in it, so no day has to be chosen.
-- NOTES.md section 12.)

§§ `Answers a row returned as a problem with the facts`

-- Row IL-03 returns LEFT for an amount of income, an inflationary amount, a
-- betterment or a sale value that is negative; of these only a negative salary
-- can arise from a household record.
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-03 reports that the facts cannot describe a case: an amount is negative` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-03 reports that the facts cannot describe a case: an amount is negative"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-06 reports that the household's facts cannot describe a family on the day` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-06 reports that the household's facts cannot describe a family on the day"
